.TH FRDP-SESSION-AGENT 8 "July 2026" "FreeRDP" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
frdp-session-agent \- per-session X11 backend for frdp-sesmand
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B frdp-session-agent
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B frdp-session-agent
is an internal per-user process started and supervised by
.BR frdp-sesmand (8).
It starts the configured Xvfb or Xorg dummy display, injects validated keyboard and pointer
input, captures bounded framebuffer tiles, and handles the supported display
and text-clipboard IPC operations.
.PP
The display server receives a random per-session MIT-MAGIC-COOKIE-1 from an
unlinked authority inode and does not listen on TCP.
.PP
It is not intended to be started manually.  Session identity, inherited
control descriptors, display geometry, and readiness reporting are supplied by
the session manager through a protected environment and inherited file
descriptors.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FRDP_SESSION_ID
Managed session identifier.
.TP
.B FRDP_CORRELATION_ID
Audit correlation identifier.
.TP
.BR DISPLAY , " FRDP_DISPLAY"
Allocated X11 display.
.TP
.B FRDP_GEOMETRY
Initial screen geometry.
.TP
.B FRDP_DISPLAY_BACKEND
Display backend selected by the session manager: xvfb or xorg-dummy.
.TP
.B FRDP_XORG_PATH
Trusted absolute raw Xorg server path for the xorg-dummy backend.
.TP
.B FRDP_XORG_CONFIG
Trusted absolute Xorg dummy configuration path.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR frdpd (8),
.BR frdp-sesmand (8),
.BR Xorg (1),
.BR Xvfb (1)
